<title>SWEDEN: Nordbanken shares rise on market rumours.</title>
<headline>Nordbanken shares rise on market rumours.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1996-12-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Swedish bank Nordbanken gained over four percent on Wednesday morning amid continuing market rumours over a possible merger with S-E-Banken.</p>
<p>At 1220 GMT Nordbanken shares were 8.5 crowns higher at 218.5 crowns. S-E-Banken shares rose 0.5 crowns to 63.50 crowns in a generally higher market with the general index up 1.11 percent.</p>
<p>&quot;The merger rumours are continuing and people think if it went ahead it would benefit Nordbanken,&quot; one broker said. &quot;But I don't think it will be this year if at all.&quot;</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1017</p>
